["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/orcidid", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[Open Researcher and Contributor ID (ORCID) iD](https://info.orcid.org/what-is-orcid/) is a unique identifier for authors and contributors in scholarly communication; as a subset of the International Standard Name Identifier (ISNI), it typically appears as a URI such as `https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1825-0097`.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RelationshipType/hasInput", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RelationshipType", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Software/SoftwarePurpose/diskImage", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The Element refers to a disk image that can be written to a disk, booted in a VM, etc. A disk image typically contains most or all of the components necessary to boot, such as bootloaders, kernels, firmware, userspace, etc.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/inspection", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "A thorough examination or checking of documentation, records, processes, or systems to confirm compliance or adherence. An inspection needs to have a defined set of acceptance criteria (e.g. a checklist), a documentation of roles involved in the inspection (e.g. to document the inspector's independence) and a clear documentation of when and how it was performed.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/HashAlgorithm/blake2b256", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/HashAlgorithm", "globalId", "", ""]
